infographic sequence-snake-steps-underline-text
data
  title Six hops, six guarantees, one invariant
  desc Only hop 1 is exactly-once; every hop after it is at-least-once, so idempotency at the consumer is what holds the chain together
  sequences
    - label 1. Order write — atomic
      desc DB row + outbox row in one txn. The event exists iff the order does. Defended by the ACID transaction.
    - label 2. Publish — at-least-once
      desc CDC relay tails the WAL into Kafka. Resuming from its log offset can re-emit a row, so dedup moves to the consumer.
    - label 3. Route — ordered per key
      desc Topic partitioned by order id keeps per-order order. Bumping partition count rehashes keys — a one-way door.
    - label 4. Process — at-least-once
      desc Consumer group commits the offset only after the handler succeeds. The fix is an idempotent handler + dedup key.
    - label 5. Quarantine — non-blocking
      desc Retry budget with backoff, then route poison messages to a DLQ so they cannot block the partition.
    - label 6. Display — eventual, honestly
      desc UI shows optimistic + pending, reconciles to confirmed or failed. The consistency window is a product surface.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
